From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000060 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: limit identity handoff to init

The KSEG0 stack probe lets /init run in QEMU, but keeping the identity return
path for every later exec makes normal Buildroot init scripts fragile. The
physical problem we are isolating is the first /init handoff, before userspace
can disable the watchdog and emit logs.

Make the SF2000 identity handoff a one-shot. The first exec keeps the ERL
identity path and copied stack workaround; later execs return through the
normal MIPS user status. This preserves the physical first-/init diagnostic
while keeping BusyBox applets and daemons on the standard Linux path.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/process.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/process.c
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@ asmlinkage void ret_from_kernel_thread(void);
 extern void sf2000_progress_mark(const char *name, unsigned int kind,
 		unsigned int value);
 extern int sf2000_rom_handoff_present(void);
+static bool sf2000_identity_handoff_used;
 
 static bool sf2000_identity_userspace_enabled(void)
 {
@@ -112,6 +113,9 @@ void start_thread(struct pt_regs * regs, unsigned long pc, unsigned long sp)
 	status = regs->cp0_status & ~(ST0_CU0|ST0_CU1|ST0_CU2|ST0_FR|KU_MASK);
 	status |= KU_USER;
 	if (sf2000_identity_userspace_enabled()) {
+		if (sf2000_identity_handoff_used)
+			goto normal_user_status;
+		sf2000_identity_handoff_used = true;
 		status |= ST0_ERL;
 		status &= ~ST0_EXL;
 		status &= ~KU_MASK;
@@ -130,6 +134,7 @@ void start_thread(struct pt_regs * regs, unsigned long pc, unsigned long sp)
 			status);
 		sf2000_progress_mark("mips-start-thread-erl-sp", 9, sp);
 	}
+normal_user_status:
 	regs->cp0_status = status;
 	lose_fpu(0);
 	clear_thread_flag(TIF_MSA_CTX_LIVE);
-- 
2.45.0
